Q: Split string into two parts after delimiter A: <p>Call on <code>preg_split()</code>. Match your delimiting operator, then forget it with <code>\K</code> so that no characters are consumed by the split. <a href="https://3v4l.org/9P8Lm#v" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Demo</a></p>
<pre class="lang-php prettyprint-override"><code>$string = 'abc==123';
var_export(
    preg_split('#==\K#', $string)
);
</code></pre>
<p>Output:</p>
<pre class="lang-php prettyprint-override"><code>array (
  0 =&gt; 'abc==',
  1 =&gt; '123',
)
</code></pre>

Q: Programmatically selecting and deselecting row in ag-grid A: <p><strong>Deselect selected rows from ag-grid react.Set properties selection single but  rowMultiSelectWithClick={true}</strong></p>
<pre><code>&lt;AgGridReact
rowSelection={&quot;single&quot;}
rowMultiSelectWithClick={true}
</code></pre>

Q: C# Add elements to Dictionary with key as string and value as another Dictionary A: <p><strong>Try Something like this</strong></p>

<pre><code>diskInfo.Add(Convert.ToString(mo["Name"]), new Dictionary&lt;string, double&gt;(spaceInfo));
</code></pre>

<p>The problem because of <strong>shallow copying.</strong>
You must perform <strong>deep copying</strong> to avoid such problems.
The copy constructor in the Dictionary class might help you solving the problem since it creates new instance from the spaceInfo object.</p>

<p>But the better way to do this is by creating class for the SpaceInformation.</p>

<pre><code>class SpaceInfo
{
    private double _size;
    private double _free;
    private double _percentFree;

    public double Size
    {
        get;
        set;
    }

    public double Free 
    {
        get;
        set;
    }

    public double PercentFree
    {
        get;
        set ;
    }

    public SpaceInfo(double size, double free)  
    {
        Size = size;
        Free = free;
        PercentFree = (free / size) * 100;
    }
}

